   faq:[{"q":"What is the exam format?","a":"The CCDV-P exam (exam guide 1.0, November 2026) has 70 scenario-based items in 120 minutes. 60 are scored and 10 are unscored trial items, which are not identified, so treat every item as scored. Items are multiple choice or multiple response, and each item states how many responses to select. It is proctored, online or at a test center, and booked through Pearson VUE."},{"q":"What score do I need to pass?","a":"A scaled score of 720 on a scale of 100 to 1,000. Anthropic does not publish how raw answers convert to the scaled score, so a percentage on this site is a guide, not a prediction. Aim for 80% or more overall and 75% or more in every domain."},{"q":"How much does the exam cost?","a":"The exam guide lists the CCDV-P exam at $175 USD, and you pay when you register through the Anthropic Partner Academy and Pearson VUE. The price shown at checkout reflects any partner discount."},{"q":"Who can take the exam?","a":"Claude certification exams are open to people who work at organizations in the Claude Partner Network. You register through the Anthropic Partner Academy, and on exam day you need a valid government-issued photo ID whose name matches your registration exactly."},{"q":"Is there a prerequisite?","a":"No. The Claude Certified Developer - Foundations certification is recommended but not required, and the guide treats its scope as assumed knowledge. The credential is awarded on exam performance alone."},{"q":"How long is the certification valid?","a":"12 months from the date it is awarded. Renewing on time is a free, unproctored assessment on the Anthropic Partner Academy; if the credential lapses, you take the full exam again at the full fee."},{"q":"Can I retake the exam?","a":"Yes, after a waiting period: 14 days after a first failed attempt, 30 days after a second and 90 days after a third, with at most four attempts in a rolling 12 months. Each attempt is paid separately."},{"q":"How close are these practice tests to the real exam?","a":"They follow the official blueprint: 70 items, 120 minutes and the same domain proportions across all eight domains, with about half the items multiple response (marked Select TWO or Select THREE). Every question is original and written from the public exam guide, so none of them comes from the real exam."},{"q":"Do I need an account?","a":"No. Everything here is free and works without signing in, and your progress is saved in your browser. Sign in only if you want to continue on another device."}],
